            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Virtual Reality Design for Science course explores the visual and human-computer interaction design process for scientific applications in immersive virtual reality. The fall 2015 version of the class, which has run on occasion for 14 years, was cross-listed at Brown University and the Rhode Island School of Design. The course feeds upon both artistic and scientific perspectives in considering the design of science-support tool prototypes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
